   $q$Listen. Bear was running to the pond and knocked over Duck's tall tower of sticks. Bear kept running and did not look back. Duck felt sad and would not play with Bear all day. The next morning, Bear went to Duck and said, I knocked your tower down, and I feel bad about it. Please forgive me. Duck smiled, and they built a new tower together. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Slow and steady wins","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Slow and steady wins"}},{"text":"Plan ahead","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Plan ahead"}},{"text":"Say you are sorry","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Say you are sorry"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Say you are sorry$q$, $q$Duck was sad until Bear came back and asked Duck to forgive the mistake. Then they were friends again. The lesson is say you are sorry.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
